{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Pre-sweep against origin/main d74d53a5ffd before spending a gate slot. Two defects in the Testing command, both of which would have made the plan's own verification a broken oracle:\n\n1. Stale package path. Both pytest targets named `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/...`. The reconciler move has landed — `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` and `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/` are both gone, replaced by `src/rebar/reconciler` and `tests/unit/reconciler/`. Collection would have errored before running anything. Corrected to `tests/unit/reconciler/`.\n\n2. Phantom test node. `::test_adr_0103_names_s3_as_cutover_owner` does not exist anywhere in the repo — `git grep adr_0103 -- '*.py'` is empty. The cited module `tests/unit/reconciler/apply/test_apply_handlers_operation_outcome.py` contains exactly one test, `test_default_context_routes_summary_only_update_through_legacy`, and it is the right target: its module docstring pins ADR 0103 at :4. Retargeted to the real node.\n\nVerified present and unchanged: `::test_adr_0095_records_the_required_sections` at `tests/unit/reconciler/test_wiki_render.py:329`; the other three pytest targets; all five cited scripts; all 20 cited ADRs.\n\nAlso applied earlier in this session: the ADR number moved 0119 -> 0121. 0119 and 0120 are both taken (`0119-mcp-surface-derived-from-library.md`, `0120-cli-verb-consolidation.md`); the plan had assumed those two stories would land as 0117/0118. 0121 is the next free number."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793477184328588001,"uuid":"7e80f344-209f-445d-ae7d-fbf2678b5a97"}